WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.890
Welcome to the Geological Museum,

2
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.200
in its anniversary year:

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.300
120 years since it was founded,

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.970
since King Carol I decided
that this would be the home

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.440
of the Geological
Institute of Romania –

6
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.310
which is what we still are today,

7
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.630
with the National Geological Museum
a department of the Institute.

8
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.930
And I'd like to invite you
to see the most beautiful

9
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.600
room in the museum, in
my opinion, which is...

10
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.520
the former Collections Room.

11
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.660
Today we call it the
Mineral Flowers Room,

12
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.340
because it houses mineral
flowers from Romania,

13
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.100
most of them, which are a treasure

14
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.320
because of their sheer beauty.

15
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.690
Unique specimens, sculpted by nature,

16
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.840
untouched by human hands,

17
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.360
exactly as they were found,

18
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.200
and still a delight to the eye today.

19
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.040
The museum officially opened
to the general public in 1990.

20
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.430
Until then, the rooms were
open only to scientists

21
00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.880
who wanted to study
particular specimens –

22
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.540
just as King Carol had wished:

23
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.210
in his decree founding the Institute,

24
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:23.600
he specified that these collections
be made available for research.

25
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.360
I've worked here since 2018.

26
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:34.740
My palaeontologist colleagues taught
me about the world of fossils,

27
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.400
and I run educational programmes

28
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.160
for pupils from primary school all
the way up to secondary school.

29
00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.390
They come through our doors
to learn what a crystal is,

30
00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.230
how a fossil forms,

31
00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:54.230
and something about the
Earth's geological past,

32
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.000
millions and millions of years ago.

33
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.460
Walking into the museum is like
opening a geology textbook

34
00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.300
and turning it page by page.
